# Bala Ged Recovery says "target card from your graveyard". Bot2's drawn Lightning Bolt is discarded at the end of turn 2,
# so on turn 3 the only card in any graveyard is in Bot2's: Bot1's Bala Ged Recovery is not offered at all (no legal target,
# CR 601.2c), and once Black Lotus is in Bot1's own graveyard a cast naming Bot2's Bolt is still refused while the same
# cast at the Lotus is the positive control. The land face (played turn 1 as Bala Ged Sanctuary) entered tapped
# and untaps for turn 3, where it taps for {G}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Bala Ged Recovery
Bala Ged Recovery
Black Lotus
Forest x4
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Bala Ged Recovery.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Bala Ged Sanctuary.Tapped = True
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Bala Ged Sanctuary.Tapped = False
? Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
! Bot1.Hand.Bala Ged Recovery.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Bala Ged Sanctuary.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {G}
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
! Bot1.Hand.Bala Ged Recovery.Cast(Bot2.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Hand.Bala Ged Recovery.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Black Lotus)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Bala Ged Recovery
Bot1.Hand = Black Lotus; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest
